    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you help me write a brief for a stakeholder? Need to explain the difference between vertical and horizontal scaling in AWS. I want to keep it simple so they get why we need Auto Scaling groups for traffic spikes, but keep it professional. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vertical scaling means increasing the capacity of a single resource, like upgrading a server's CPU or RAM. Horizontal scaling, conversely, involves adding more instances of a resource to distribute the load across multiple servers. We use Auto Scaling groups to implement horizontal scaling, allowing our application to automatically add or remove instances to handle unexpected traffic spikes efficiently and maintain performance. This approach ensures reliability and cost optimization under variable load conditions.",
      "source": "target",
