    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Auto Scaling groups monitor key performance metrics to trigger new instances when necessary. Common metrics we track include CPU utilization, where if the average CPU across our current instances consistently exceeds a set threshold—say, 70%—the group automatically launches more servers. Conversely, when traffic subsides, the group scales down to save on operational costs. This automated responsiveness is what allows us to handle spikes gracefully while remaining cost-efficient.",
      "source": "target",
